# Pending Feature Docs Maintenance

Whenever you complete, partially complete, or discover work for this POS system, update the matching pending list before finishing the task:

- Backend work → `docs/pending feature/backend.md`
- Frontend work → `docs/pending feature/frontend.md`

## How to update

1. **Done:** Change `[ ]` to `[x]` **and** wrap the full item text in markdown strikethrough so completed work is easy to scan past:

   ```markdown
   - [x] ~~**Short title** — Feature NNN: brief note.~~
   ```

   For Phase A (or similar) status table cells that are done, strikethrough the status text the same way (`~~**Done** — …~~`).

2. **Partial:** Leave `[ ]` (no strikethrough) but add a one-line note under the item describing what remains.
3. **New gaps:** Append new unchecked items when implementation reveals follow-ups (do not invent scope the user did not discuss).
4. **Promoted:** If an item becomes a formal `docs/features/00N-*` triad, note that path next to the item and keep `[ ]` (no strikethrough) until shipped, then apply the Done pattern above.

Do this in the same session as the feature work—do not wait for the user to ask. Still respect frontend/backend separation for code commits; doc updates to these pending files may ship with the side that completed the work.
